To answer the question, we need to write a SPARQL query that traverses the six AAS domains and finds the engineering resources linked to the canonical AssetIdentifier `https://aas.example.com/TI101`. We will use the SHACL property paths and constraints to filter the results.

Here is the query:
```sparql
PREFIX aas: <https://example.org/aas/>
PREFIX dexpifunc: <https://example.org/dexpifunc/>
PREFIX ecad: <https://example.org/ecad/>
PREFIX engbom: <https://example.org/engbom/>
PREFIX assetinv: <https://example.org/assetinventory/>
PREFIX productcat: <https://example.org/productcatalog/>
PREFIX opcua: <https://example.org/opcuaconnectivity/>

SELECT ?resource ?domain
WHERE {
  ?resource aas:SMC .
  ?resource aas:hasAssetIdentifier ?assetid .
  FILTER (?assetid = "https://aas.example.com/TI101") .

  # DEXPI function and identifier
  OPTIONAL { ?resource dexpifunc:hasFunction ?func . }
  OPTIONAL { ?resource dexpifunc:hasIdentifier ?ident . }

  # ECAD device and local tag
  OPTIONAL { ?resource ecad:hasDevice ?device . }
  OPTIONAL { ?resource ecad:hasLocalTag ?tag . }

  # Engineering BOM items
  OPTIONAL { ?resource engbom:hasItem ?item . }

  # AssetInventory logical asset
  OPTIONAL { ?resource assetinv:hasAsset ?asset . }

  # ProductCatalog product candidate and physical-installation status
  OPTIONAL { ?resource productcat:hasProduct ?product . }
  OPTIONAL { ?resource productcat:hasPhysicalInstallationStatus ?status . }

  # OPC UA operational signal/node and mapping provenance/status
  OPTIONAL { ?resource opcua:hasServer ?server . }
  OPTIONAL { ?resource opcua:hasSignal ?signal . }
  OPTIONAL { ?resource opcua:hasMapping ?mapping . }

  # Filter verified graph links
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?resource aas:hasAssertion ?assertion . }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?resource aas:hasProvisionalAssertion ?assertion . }

  # Filter provisional or unverified assertions
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?resource aas:hasProvisionalAssertion ?assertion . }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?resource aas:hasUnverifiedAssertion ?assertion . }

  # Filter XMEAS9 observations for run 10cfb1d1-2984-4932-8207-dc430ed60c2b between simulation seconds 0 and 600
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?resource aas:hasXMEAS9Observation ?observation . }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?observation aas:hasRun "10cfb1d1-2984-4932-8207-dc430ed60c2b" . }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?observation aas:hasSimulationSeconds [ >= 0, <= 600 ] . }
}
```
This query uses the `OPTIONAL` keyword to include the optional property paths and constraints for each domain. The `FILTER` keyword is used to filter the results based on the constraints.

Note that this query is quite complex and may take some time to execute. Also, the query assumes that the AAS domains are properly configured and that the SHACL property paths and constraints are correctly defined.

The query will return a list of engineering resources linked to the canonical AssetIdentifier `https://aas.example.com/TI101`, along with the domain in which each resource is located. The results will be filtered to exclude provisional or unverified assertions and XMEAS9 observations for the specified run and simulation seconds.
